From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 03:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: dma: sun50i-a64-dma: add the A733 controller

The A733 DMA controller takes the A100's two clocks (bus, mbus) and one
reset, and its channel count comes from the device tree. It has no
fallback compatible: its interrupt registers are per channel, where every
compatible in this binding has global ones, so no existing driver config
runs it correctly.

Assisted-by: Claude
---
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/dma/allwinner,sun50i-a64-dma.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/dma/allwinner,sun50i-a64-dma.yaml
@@ -25,6 +25,7 @@ properties:
           - allwinner,sun50i-a64-dma
           - allwinner,sun50i-a100-dma
           - allwinner,sun50i-h6-dma
+          - allwinner,sun60i-a733-dma
       - items:
           - const: allwinner,sun8i-r40-dma
           - const: allwinner,sun50i-a64-dma
@@ -67,6 +68,7 @@ if:
           - allwinner,sun20i-d1-dma
           - allwinner,sun50i-a100-dma
           - allwinner,sun50i-h6-dma
+          - allwinner,sun60i-a733-dma
 
 then:
   properties:
